{"author": "Kahlil Gibran", "author_id": 17, "body": "The deeper that sorrow carves into your being, the more joy you can contain.", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "7247a9b08297d7fc029b6a6ded2beb0f61693eef4bfa7193f399b2c88cce89d4", "checked_ebook_id": 58585, "checked_end": 19943, "checked_start": 19867, "checked_wikisource_oldid": null, "id": 61, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "The Prophet", "source_location": "“On Joy and Sorrow”", "source_url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/58585", "speaker": null, "status": "live", "themes": ["love", "calm"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 18}
{"author": "Rabindranath Tagore", "author_id": 9, "body": "Let life be beautiful like summer flowers and death like autumn leaves.", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "f589a830a307b6844504e6b03b764854b09352f05ff2c6db291cc9d7dc8ab7cb", "checked_ebook_id": 6524, "checked_end": 7379, "checked_start": 7308, "checked_wikisource_oldid": null, "id": 62, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "Stray Birds", "source_location": "Stray Birds (1916), no. 82", "source_url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/6524", "speaker": null, "status": "live", "themes": ["time", "nature"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 10}
{"author": "Henry David Thoreau", "author_id": 8, "body": "If you have built castles in the air, your work need not be lost; that is where they should be. Now put the foundations under them.", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "9694e150f384e231fab223599597c6d3c8a95688ea591c335d454cc6e8990cec", "checked_ebook_id": 205, "checked_end": 565773, "checked_start": 565642, "checked_wikisource_oldid": null, "id": 63, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "Walden", "source_location": "Conclusion", "source_url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/205", "speaker": null, "status": "live", "themes": ["purpose", "courage"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 8}
{"author": "Kahlil Gibran", "author_id": 17, "body": "Your children are not your children.\nThey are the sons and daughters of Life’s longing for itself.", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "7247a9b08297d7fc029b6a6ded2beb0f61693eef4bfa7193f399b2c88cce89d4", "checked_ebook_id": 58585, "checked_end": 11375, "checked_start": 11276, "checked_wikisource_oldid": null, "id": 64, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "The Prophet", "source_location": "“On Children”", "source_url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/58585", "speaker": null, "status": "live", "themes": ["love"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 18}
{"author": "Henry David Thoreau", "author_id": 8, "body": "If a man does not keep pace with his companions, perhaps it is because he hears a different drummer. Let him step to the music which he hears, however measured or far away.", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "9694e150f384e231fab223599597c6d3c8a95688ea591c335d454cc6e8990cec", "checked_ebook_id": 205, "checked_end": 569482, "checked_start": 569310, "checked_wikisource_oldid": null, "id": 65, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "Walden", "source_location": "Conclusion", "source_url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/205", "speaker": null, "status": "live", "themes": ["self", "courage"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 8}
{"author": "Rabindranath Tagore", "author_id": 9, "body": "Every child comes with the message that God is not yet discouraged of man.", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "f589a830a307b6844504e6b03b764854b09352f05ff2c6db291cc9d7dc8ab7cb", "checked_ebook_id": 6524, "checked_end": 7002, "checked_start": 6928, "checked_wikisource_oldid": null, "id": 66, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "Stray Birds", "source_location": "Stray Birds (1916), no. 77", "source_url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/6524", "speaker": null, "status": "live", "themes": ["love", "purpose"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 10}
{"author": "John Donne", "author_id": 60, "body": "Any man’s death diminishes me, because I am involved in mankind, and therefore never send to know for whom the bell tolls; it tolls for thee.", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "7b24e19490af87aa34807a41b374ace4dfe925f2e7535caa9d1418497066f520", "checked_ebook_id": null, "checked_end": 2769, "checked_start": 2628, "checked_wikisource_oldid": 13696894, "id": 67, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "Devotions upon Emergent Occasions", "source_location": "Meditation XVII", "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Devotions/Meditation_17", "speaker": null, "status": "live", "themes": ["love"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 60}
{"author": "Ralph Waldo Emerson", "author_id": 1, "body": "A friend is a person with whom I may be sincere. Before him I may think aloud.", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "b5e2d54d63f99e855fc4726322f2a6520288cfeb32c0cbd5c9c8a9d7b0b08dd1", "checked_ebook_id": 2944, "checked_end": 228306, "checked_start": 228228, "checked_wikisource_oldid": null, "id": 68, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "Friendship", "source_location": "“Friendship”, Essays: First Series (1841)", "source_url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/2944", "speaker": null, "status": "live", "themes": ["love"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 71}
{"author": "Marcus Aurelius", "author_id": 11, "body": "Do not act as if thou wert going to live ten thousand years. Death hangs over thee. While thou livest, while it is in thy power, be good.", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "c94855366014552f7d493b94db0c6484a36408179069fa54871d4c3a87f8dc75", "checked_ebook_id": 15877, "checked_end": 185488, "checked_start": 185351, "checked_wikisource_oldid": null, "id": 69, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "Meditations (trans. George Long)", "source_location": "Book IV, §17", "source_url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/15877", "speaker": null, "status": "live", "themes": ["time", "purpose"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 12}
{"author": "The Buddha", "author_id": 32, "body": "Hatred does not cease by hatred at any time: hatred ceases by love, this is an old rule.", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "a08b9e2b6834a4c786711605f6da4973e956301f778c7a9c41704d09e19d8a34", "checked_ebook_id": 2017, "checked_end": 1981, "checked_start": 1893, "checked_wikisource_oldid": null, "id": 70, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "Dhammapada (trans. F. Max Müller)", "source_location": "Chapter I (The Twin-Verses), verse 5", "source_url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/2017", "speaker": null, "status": "live", "themes": ["love", "calm"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 32}
{"author": "Michel de Montaigne", "author_id": 35, "body": "When I play with my cat who knows whether I do not make her more sport than she makes me?", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "bde3d40574c053bd6f44c4136e9269aeb5470d9e7026e35de9bfced800789da1", "checked_ebook_id": 3600, "checked_end": 1230964, "checked_start": 1230875, "checked_wikisource_oldid": null, "id": 71, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "Apology for Raimond Sebond (trans. Charles Cotton)", "source_location": "Essays, Book II, ch. XII, “Apology for Raimond Sebond”", "source_url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/3600", "speaker": null, "status": "live", "themes": ["nature", "self"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 83}
{"author": "George Eliot", "author_id": 19, "body": "The growing good of the world is partly dependent on unhistoric acts; and that things are not so ill with you and me as they might have been, is half owing to the number who lived faithfully a hidden life, and rest in unvisited tombs.", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "3f7f17746cb8400b5241d37f799bdfc867a0b35b7bb0ae4757b8f1ceda78ba05", "checked_ebook_id": 145, "checked_end": 1780172, "checked_start": 1779938, "checked_wikisource_oldid": null, "id": 72, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "Middlemarch", "source_location": "Finale, last sentence", "source_url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/145", "speaker": null, "status": "live", "themes": ["purpose", "love"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 20}
{"author": "Charlotte Brontë", "author_id": 12, "body": "Do you think, because I am poor, obscure, plain, and little, I am soulless and heartless? You think wrong!", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "1c2bd174cfa83d2f9603a8ce8c4186402eed3ea0ea39bfd534f9d67ccd0aa0fb", "checked_ebook_id": 1260, "checked_end": 567876, "checked_start": 567769, "checked_wikisource_oldid": null, "id": 73, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "Jane Eyre", "source_location": "Chapter 23, Jane to Rochester", "source_url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/1260", "speaker": "Jane", "status": "live", "themes": ["self", "courage"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 13}
{"author": "Paul Laurence Dunbar", "author_id": 27, "body": "We wear the mask that grins and lies,\nIt hides our cheeks and shades our eyes,—\nThis debt we pay to human guile.", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "2a4d9b93247a4ef21b1067471ad93e7984d73ea74940af6c3c9cdccec769509e", "checked_ebook_id": 18338, "checked_end": 181351, "checked_start": 181234, "checked_wikisource_oldid": null, "id": 74, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "We Wear the Mask", "source_location": "“We Wear the Mask”, lines 1–3", "source_url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/18338", "speaker": null, "status": "live", "themes": ["self"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 81}
{"author": "Socrates", "author_id": 28, "body": "The hour of departure has arrived, and we go our ways—I to die, and you to live. Which is better God only knows.", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "f1db65c8de95a3d3cb182c126d59939213b1c02195a9281efada098070e06362", "checked_ebook_id": 1656, "checked_end": 85796, "checked_start": 85684, "checked_wikisource_oldid": null, "id": 75, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "Plato’s Apology (trans. Benjamin Jowett)", "source_location": "Apology 42a, Socrates’ last words to the jury", "source_url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/1656", "speaker": null, "status": "live", "themes": ["time", "courage"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 29}
{"author": "L. M. Montgomery", "author_id": 10, "body": "I’m so glad I live in a world where there are Octobers.", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "99e1d25aa5ba87a999d5938743520983efa8e5c210bdbd6b5cd5a0320d79afe8", "checked_ebook_id": 45, "checked_end": 216563, "checked_start": 216508, "checked_wikisource_oldid": null, "id": 76, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "Anne of Green Gables", "source_location": "Chapter XVI, Anne", "source_url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/45", "speaker": "Anne", "status": "live", "themes": ["nature", "time"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 11}
