{"author": "William Blake", "author_id": 48, "body": "Man was made for Joy & Woe\nAnd when this we rightly Know\nThro the World we safely go\nJoy & woe are woven fine\nA Clothing for the soul divine", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "15cf0e2ebe078681c4f7b5ba9b0406a18740f428141a245be3815e8e73ad8cf1", "checked_ebook_id": null, "checked_end": 2031, "checked_start": 1891, "checked_wikisource_oldid": 7160442, "id": 89, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "Auguries of Innocence", "source_location": "Auguries of Innocence, lines 55–59 (Pickering Manuscript, unpunctuated)", "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Pickering_Manuscript/Auguries_of_Innocence", "speaker": null, "status": "live", "themes": ["calm", "love"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 48}
{"author": "Confucius", "author_id": 22, "body": "What you do not want done to yourself, do not do to others.", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "120d414eafa89340d9329a37a10a87eecc997e7e40514ae4512113b76c25a17d", "checked_ebook_id": 3330, "checked_end": 125310, "checked_start": 125250, "checked_wikisource_oldid": null, "id": 90, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "Analects (trans. James Legge)", "source_location": "Book XV (Wei Ling Kung), ch. XXIII", "source_url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/3330", "speaker": null, "status": "live", "themes": ["love"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 23}
{"author": "Mary Wollstonecraft", "author_id": 38, "body": "It is justice, not charity, that is wanting in the world!", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "b26147da37e38033ecb2e0a0e701764c3c42a2dd4b12093839d43c00a0d2c25d", "checked_ebook_id": 3420, "checked_end": 186263, "checked_start": 186206, "checked_wikisource_oldid": null, "id": 91, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "A Vindication of the Rights of Woman", "source_location": "Chapter 9", "source_url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/3420", "speaker": null, "status": "live", "themes": ["purpose", "love"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 38}
{"author": "Sara Teasdale", "author_id": 34, "body": "Spend all you have for loveliness,\nBuy it and never count the cost;\nFor one white singing hour of peace\nCount many a year of strife well lost.", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "4e5593227f225b62c731acc7597c6c5bb75fc249103fcb8d07dada1685780248", "checked_ebook_id": 442, "checked_end": 3127, "checked_start": 2977, "checked_wikisource_oldid": null, "id": 92, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "Barter", "source_location": "“Barter”, stanza 3, lines 1–4", "source_url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/442", "speaker": null, "status": "live", "themes": ["love", "courage"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 34}
{"author": "The Buddha", "author_id": 32, "body": "As a solid rock is not shaken by the wind, wise people falter not amidst blame and praise.", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "a08b9e2b6834a4c786711605f6da4973e956301f778c7a9c41704d09e19d8a34", "checked_ebook_id": 2017, "checked_end": 13914, "checked_start": 13824, "checked_wikisource_oldid": null, "id": 93, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "Dhammapada (trans. F. Max Müller)", "source_location": "Chapter VI (The Wise Man), verse 81", "source_url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/2017", "speaker": null, "status": "live", "themes": ["calm", "courage"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 32}
{"author": "Lao Tzu", "author_id": 13, "body": "He who knows other men is discerning; he who knows himself is intelligent. He who overcomes others is strong; he who overcomes himself is mighty.", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "25d7edc3630ee9a7b540927bf65a849182b4a43873fd0d93e661ab9d710f5744", "checked_ebook_id": 216, "checked_end": 24474, "checked_start": 24328, "checked_wikisource_oldid": null, "id": 94, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "Tao Te Ching (trans. James Legge)", "source_location": "Chapter 33, §1", "source_url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/216", "speaker": null, "status": "live", "themes": ["self", "courage"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 14}
{"author": "Paul Laurence Dunbar", "author_id": 27, "body": "It is not a carol of joy or glee,\nBut a prayer that he sends from his heart’s deep core,\nBut a plea, that upward to Heaven he flings—\nI know why the caged bird sings!", "body_format": [], "checked_at": "2026-10-29T01:59:19Z", "checked_body_sha256": "2a4d9b93247a4ef21b1067471ad93e7984d73ea74940af6c3c9cdccec769509e", "checked_ebook_id": 18338, "checked_end": 231963, "checked_start": 231788, "checked_wikisource_oldid": null, "id": 95, "is_starter": false, "kind": "quote", "match_kind": "exact", "source": "Sympathy", "source_location": "“Sympathy”, stanza 3, last 4 lines (Lyrics of the Hearthside, 1899)", "source_url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/18338", "speaker": null, "status": "live", "themes": ["courage", "self"], "verifier_version": "5eac8affab7ea3d11dd1c66a4a3b48aaf08a65e5", "work_id": 80}
